PATCH 181: reconstruct the per-node display-list PAINT handler FUN_0000_584a (asm 0x584a-0x5888).

584a is dispatched by 209e's display-list walk via `fist_icall_near(0x0,off)()` with NO register args.
Ghidra kept only the TAIL (0x5870-0x5888: c61a(ax); bump DGROUP:[bx]/[bx+2]; nested c6c8; restore) and
DROPPED the whole HEAD (0x584a-0x586f, which computes the c61a arg ax from the nested element), and it
base-lost bx (treated the dropped param_1 as a host pointer -> *(int*)(param_1+4) wild-deref -> SIGSEGV,
param_1=0x8054039).  bx (node offset) is published by 209e to DGROUP:0x3e08, bp (walk base) to
g_fist_paintbp (patch 142); SS=DS=DGROUP.  Reconstructed as a faithful transliteration.

Reached only on the ACCEPT mission cascade (the menu's display-list nodes never select the 584a paint
method, else the pre-patch wild deref would crash the 19 flows -> they are 19/19) -> behaviour-neutral.
Sources stay pristine; fist.c via build/.

